---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Labs"
  description="Where I try things out: watch apps, prototypes and working tools, built because the problem was in front of me and the tool was not."
>
  <main class="reading" id="main">
    <section class="block insight-page">
      <p class="kicker">TROi</p>
      <h1>Labs</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        This is where I experiment. Most of it starts the same way: something comes up over lunch or by the coffee
        machine and turns out to be a problem several people share — usually one I have run into myself.
        Work and life outside it both throw up that moment — something is harder than it needs to be, and the tool
        that would have helped does not exist. The quickest way to find out whether an idea answers it is to build the
        smallest version and use it for a while. And some of it is here for no better reason than that it was fun to
        make.
      </p>

      <p>
        Some of what is here ships: two Garmin watch apps are in public beta, and a set of watch faces is on the
        Connect IQ store. The rest runs here and gets used, which is exactly the point at which it becomes
        impossible to tell whether something is genuinely useful or just fits the way one person works.
      </p>

      <p>
        So I put them up, unfinished and clearly labelled. Each page says where that thing actually is — shipped,
        prototype, or part specification — and the three faces at the bottom take one press and tell me what to
        take further and what to let mature a while longer. If you have more to say than a face can carry,{' '}
        <a href="/contact/">write to me</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="tool-note">
        <strong>New:</strong> the two watch apps are out as free public betas on Garmin Connect IQ —{' '}
        <a href="https://apps.garmin.com/apps/35125b1c-d056-4856-9962-2b1652e3f0a3" rel="noopener">FlowLens</a>, on work/life balance, and{' '}
        <a href="https://apps.garmin.com/apps/eb8a524d-445f-409a-bb51-c2a0a742dabe" rel="noopener">FlowMission</a>, on an hour you have anyway. Both need people wearing them,
        so install one and tell me what it got right and what it got wrong.
      </p>

      <ul class="tool-list">
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Public beta on Garmin Connect IQ</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/flowlens/">FlowLens</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            Work/life balance metrics on the wrist. Four questions about the week that people already ask
            themselves and mostly answer by guessing, answered from your own history.{' '}
            <a href="https://apps.garmin.com/apps/35125b1c-d056-4856-9962-2b1652e3f0a3" rel="noopener">Install it</a> and help test it.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Public beta on Garmin Connect IQ</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/flowmission/">FlowMission</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            An hour in a city you don't know, or a race you have a time for. The watch works out what is
            possible and hands back one instruction, plus a promise that you get back — and somebody who is
            told when you don't.{' '}
            <a href="https://apps.garmin.com/apps/eb8a524d-445f-409a-bb51-c2a0a742dabe" rel="noopener">Install it</a> and help test it.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Coming soon to TestFlight</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/sammans/">Sammans</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            A coach for personal growth that makes your relationships stronger. It helps you find direction and a goal, picks the tools, and keeps the everyday life puzzle in view. It replaces Livspusslet.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Working prototype</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/cambium/">Cambium</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            An organization moves at the speed of what it has already settled. That was always true; agents
            made it visible. A person who reaches an undecided question guesses and carries on, and the cost
            surfaces months later. An agent stops and asks — so the missing decision shows up on the day it is
            missing, and the answer serves whoever comes next, person or machine.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Working prototype</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/bordvakt/">Bordvakt</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            Some restaurants release a month of tables in one batch and lose them in minutes. This waits for
            the release.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="marginalia-label">Working prototype</p>
          <p class="tool-name"><a href="/tools/cutover/">Cutover Control Center</a></p>
          <p class="tool-line">
            Hundreds of moving parts, and a plan that can start anywhere — typed in here or dropped in from a
            spreadsheet. What it adds is the answer to what is running, what is late and who is waiting.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="tool-aside-head">On the wrist</h2>
      <p class="tool-aside">
        FlowLens and FlowMission live beside a handful of Garmin watch faces and data fields I have published
        under the same name — the Grande family, built while learning what the watch can and cannot do. They are on
        the Connect IQ store as{' '}
        <a href="https://apps.garmin.com/developer/6e0b12d9-69d1-4f82-be68-6a71025128c5/apps" rel="noopener">Apps by TROi</a>, and they are worth a try if you wear a Garmin.
      </p>

      <figure class="wrist-figure">
        <a href="https://apps.garmin.com/developer/6e0b12d9-69d1-4f82-be68-6a71025128c5/apps" rel="noopener">
          <img
            src="/tools/grande-watch-faces.webp"
            width="1850"
            height="1808"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="The Grande family on a Garmin watch: the Complication, Digital, Pulse, Orbit, Words, Expedition, Move, Swimrun, Trail, Ultra and Tri watch faces, the Expedition Card widget, and the Cutoff and Multisport data fields."
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Grande — watch faces, a widget and data fields for Garmin.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wrist-figure {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
  }
  .wrist-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .wrist-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  .tool-note {
    margin: 1.8rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--moss);
    background: var(--paper-deep);
  }
  .tool-aside-head {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2.8rem 0 0.7rem;
  }
  .tool-aside {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
  .tool-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0;
  }
  .tool-list li {
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--mist);
  }
  .tool-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mist);
  }
  .tool-name {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .tool-line {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--bark);
  }
</style>
